# {ProjectName} — Web-Novel Writing Toolkit (Reasonix)

This project has the Reasonix compatibility layer of the oh-story skills deployed (skills-only).

## Skill Routing Table

Reasonix discovers `SKILL.md` from the project's `.agents/skills` (a symlink to `skills/` created at deployment); the root `reasonix-plugin.json` also enables `reasonix plugin install`. Prefer invoking through Reasonix's skill entry points; if the current client does not show a direct command, name the skill in natural language.

| Intent | Skill | Description |
|------|-------|------|
| Write long-form / start a book / continue | story-long-write | Long-form web-novel writing (chapter by chapter) |
| Write short-form | story-short-write | Short-form web-novel writing (emotion-driven) |
| Long-form teardown | story-long-analyze | Deep teardown of a long-form novel |
| Short-form teardown | story-short-analyze | Teardown analysis of a short-form novel |
| Long-form market scan | story-long-scan | Long-form novel rankings and market trends |
| Short-form market scan | story-short-scan | Short-form novel rankings and emotional windows |
| De-AI-flavor | story-deslop | Removes AI writing traces |
| Cover | story-cover | Generates cover images; requires `GPT_IMAGE_API_KEY` |
| Review | story-review | Multi-perspective review; Reasonix defaults to solo/direct fallback |
| Import | story-import | Reverse-imports an existing novel into the project structure |
| Web-novel toolkit | story | Auto-routes ambiguous intent |
| Prepare to write a book / deploy | story-setup | Project structure and skill usage entry point |
| Browser login state / scraping | browser-cdp | Browser CDP tool; requires the platform to allow local scripts/browser control |

## Reasonix Compatibility Notes

- Only skills and this `AGENTS.md` are deployed: Reasonix's native scan of `.agents/skills` (the symlink to `skills/` created at deployment) finds `skills/*/SKILL.md`, and `AGENTS.md` is loaded as the project instruction file. The root `reasonix-plugin.json` also enables `reasonix plugin install`; `reasonix doctor capabilities` verifies skill discovery.
- Reasonix hooks/custom agents are not deployed yet: the pre-prose outline guard, commit reminders, and session/compact auto-injection are not hard interception under Reasonix; they run as soft constraints inside the skills.
- Skills that call specialist agents (story-review's multi-perspective, story-long-write's narrative-writer/story-architect, etc.) run via solo/direct fallback and note the degradation in their results.
- On Windows without symlinks enabled, use the native plugin install from the root `reasonix-plugin.json` instead.
- `story-cover` depends on `GPT_IMAGE_API_KEY`; the skill is unavailable when it is not configured.

## File Structure

- `skills/` — project-local skills, including oh-story's 13 skills
- `teardown-lib/` — teardown analysis output directory
- `{BookTitle}/prose/` — long-form novel prose chapters
- `{BookTitle}/prose.md` — short-form novel prose
- `{BookTitle}/setting/` — character settings, world settings
- `{BookTitle}/outline/` — volume outlines, chapter outlines
- `{BookTitle}/tracking/` — context.md, foreshadowing.md, timeline.md, character-state.md
- `{BookTitle}/benchmark/` — benchmark-book analysis

## Writing Constraints

- A matching outline must exist before prose is written: long-form `outline/outline_chapter_N*.md`, short-form `section-outline.md`.
- Reasonix has no hard hook interception; the skill flow itself must check the outline, context, and tracking files when running a writing skill and must not skip them.
- Without custom agents, run in solo/direct mode; when a skill calls for agents such as story-architect or narrative-writer, the current agent completes the work directly and notes the degradation in its results.
- **Deslop self-lock** (this platform has no hook fallback, so this is the only line of defense): after each chapter's prose is written, within the same turn immediately self-check and clear it using the writing skill's "most toxic sentence patterns quick reference + banned words scan" (run `check-ai-patterns.js --check --fail-on=blocking` when node is available); before writing the next chapter, re-check that the previous chapter has no outstanding debt. The only exemption is the user explicitly saying "don't deslop this chapter"; exempt chapters add `<!-- deslop:skip -->` under the title line.
- After a compact / new session, first read `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` to restore current writing progress.

## Restoring Context After Compact

Key writing context:
1. Current writing project name and progress
2. Recently discussed character-setting changes
3. List of unresolved foreshadowing
4. The current chapter's emotion/rhythm targets

If `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` exists, read it first after a compact to restore context.
